Beowulf is a 2007 American animated fantasy action film produced and directed by Robert Zemeckis, written by Neil Gaiman and Roger Avary, based on the Old English epic poem
Beowulf, and featuring the voices of Ray Winstone, Anthony Hopkins, Robin Wright, Brendan Gleeson, John Malkovich, Crispin Glover, Alison Lohman, and Angelina Jolie.

11
01:14:24,705 --> 01:14:30,705
The film depicts a modern interpretation of the poem, with
certain changes to aspects of its story.

12
01:21:10,588 --> 01:21:16,588
It was produced by Shangri-La Entertainment and Zemeckis's ImageMovers and features characters animated using
motion-capture animation, which was previously used in The Polar Express (2004) and Monster House (2006).

13
